    "field": "Climate change",
    "problem": "The absence of systems for monitoring global CO\u2082 emissions in real-time, with annual reports being too slow and atmospheric/satellite data too uncertain, prevents the timely assessment of rapid changes caused by major disruptions like the COVID-19 pandemic.",
    "method": "To estimate daily CO2 emission changes, the authors developed a confinement index based on government policies and combined it with near-real-time activity data for six economic sectors across 69 countries and multiple subnational regions, representing 97% of global emissions.",
    "task": "The task is to estimate the daily decrease in global CO\u2082 emissions during COVID-19 forced confinements by compiling government policies and near-real-time activity data for different economic sectors, compensating for the lack of direct real-time emissions monitoring.",
